            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Keishing",
                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "Last supported for legacy REST  https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc-test-automation/releases/tag/v4.0-stable\n\nwe will be removing those test ahead.. so lets not add anything specific REST tags.. Thanks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Igor Kanyuka",
                        "email": "ifelmail@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ifel"
                    },
                    "message": "I see. Should I just remove these tests instead of tagging them?\n\nIf not, what's the harm of tagging them? The problem with these is, I need an efficient way to exclude these from runs and tagging is the best way for that (plus, it will allow to find the tests to remove)."
                }
            ],
